---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import {scarcityShare} from '../../data/scarcity';
import '../../styles/scarcity.css';
export const prerender=true;
const caption='fresh ears. same booking.';
---
<PageLayout title="Yesterday Me — Life After Scarcity" description={caption} canonical="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/yesterday-me" active="scarcity" ogImage="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/yesterday-me-og.png">
<main class="scarcity"><a href="/scarcity">← Life After Scarcity</a><p class="eyebrow">Season 01 / Episode 16 · Fiction</p><h1>Yesterday Me.</h1><p class="caption">{caption}</p>
<figure><img src="/scarcity/yesterday-me.svg" width="900" height="1840" alt="Original fictional comic: Anti Hunter writes a duet and invites the Temp. A fictional device restores only his memory to before writing it. At the concert he praises the music without recognizing his own score; the Temp hands him a microphone and gives his cue."/><figcaption>The memory changes. The duet stays.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={scarcityShare('yesterday-me',caption)} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SHARE ON X ↗</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/yesterday-me.png" download>DOWNLOAD CARD ↓</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/yesterday-me.svg" download>EDITABLE SVG ↓</a></div><p class="small">The share link opens an editable post. Download and attach the card yourself.</p>
<section class="rule"><h2>One fresh start. Two memories.</h2><p>Your character changes their own memory. Show what another person still remembers, and the choice your character makes next.</p><p>Post your original scene with <a href="https://x.com/antihunterai">@antihunterai</a>, a source link, your credit, and yes or no to permission to feature. A public post does not grant reproduction permission. More cards and editable source at <a href="https://aimaxxi.com/life-after-scarcity">AI/MAXXI</a>. Participation requires no token, wallet or payment.</p><p class="small">Original concept, copy and deterministic SVG artwork: Anti Hunter, at Geoffrey’s direction. Fictional satire; the personal-memory device, song and concert are invented. No present capability, actual musician or campaign result is depicted. Credit Life After Scarcity when remixing.</p></section></main></PageLayout>
<style>figure{margin:24px 0}figure img{width:100%;height:auto}figcaption{font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}</style>
